{meta title='Chord boxes'/}
<p class="nt-lead">A chord of a guitar or a ukulele drawn as the box of a chord chart: the strings
standing up, the frets across, a dot for every finger and a bar where one finger lies across
the strings, <code>o</code> over a string played open and <code>×</code> over one not played,
the note of every string below. A chord name - C, Am, F#m7, Bbmaj7, Dsus4, G7/B - is drawn in
the shape a player learns first, or a shape found for it from its notes; a shape can be given
as its frets.</p>

<p class="nt-tag">Written <code>{open/}notation:chord 'Am'/{close/}</code> - bare, <code>{open/}chord{close/}</code>
is the chord diagram of the charts. <code>instrument='ukulele'</code> tunes it G C E A,
<code>frets='x32010'</code> gives the shape.</p>

{examples/}
